IMPORT prelude

-- Public Order Act 2009 (Singapore) -- when a public assembly or procession needs notice and a permit (ss 2, 3, 5, 14, 46), the
-- foreign-participation ground for refusing a permit (s 7(2)(h), (4)), permit duration (s 9), appeals (s 11), the offences of
-- organising and taking part (ss 15, 16), their defences (s 17), immunity for lawful participants (s 19), special notice of large
-- events (s 6A), move-on directions (ss 34 to 37), directions to delete films of law enforcement (s 38), the liability of an
-- owner or occupier (s 42), and the penalties and composition limit for those offences (s 41).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/POA2009.txt, incorporating
-- amendments up to 1 December 2021; the latest annotations in the body are 26/2018 and "Act 12 of 2020 wef 01/10/2025" (the
-- latter in Part 3, not encoded).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to what an organiser, a participant, a
-- bystander with a phone, or an owner of premises meets. Not encoded: the contents of the notice (s 6(3)), the Commissioner's
-- general discretion to grant or refuse (s 7(1), (2)(a) to (g)), conditions (s 8), prohibited areas and orders (ss 12, 13) beyond
-- their effect, Part 3 (special events security) entirely, arrest, bodies corporate, service and regulations. The prescribed
-- notice periods and the prescribed crowd size for s 6A are in regulations, which were not retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Public Order Act 2009 -- assemblies and processions`

§§ `2, 5, 14, 46 -- when notice and a permit are required`

-- s 2(1): an "assembly" is a gathering of persons "the purpose (or one of the purposes) of which is -- (a) to demonstrate support for
-- or opposition to the views or actions of any person, group of persons or any government; (b) to publicise a cause or campaign;
-- or (c) to mark or commemorate any event", and "includes a demonstration by a person alone" for any of those purposes. A
-- "procession" is a march of 2 or more for the same purposes, and includes "a march by a person alone" for them.
-- "public assembly": held in a public place "or to which members of the public in general are invited, induced or permitted to
-- attend". "public procession": "in, to or from a public place".
-- s 5(1): a public assembly or procession "must not take place unless" the Commissioner is notified under s 6 and a permit is
-- granted under s 7, and it is not prohibited under s 12 or 13. (2): not for (a) one exempted under s 46, or (b) one "within any
-- part of an unrestricted area not falling within a special event area of an enhanced security special event".
-- s 14(1): in an unrestricted area "no notice under section 6, and no permit under section 7, is required".
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `support for or opposition to a person, group or government`
    `publicising a cause or campaign`
    `commemorating an event`
    `recreation or entertainment only`

DECLARE Gathering HAS
    `purpose` IS A Purpose
    `is a march` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the public in general are invited` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an unrestricted area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within an enhanced security special event area` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempted by Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is a regulated purpose` IF
    CONSIDER `the purpose`
    WHEN `recreation or entertainment only` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- Number of persons is not modelled: a lone demonstrator or marcher is within both definitions for the same three purposes.
GIVEN `the gathering` IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a public assembly or public procession` IF
        `the purpose is a regulated purpose` (`the gathering`'s `purpose`)
    AND (    `the gathering`'s `held in a public place`
         OR  (    (NOT `the gathering`'s `is a march`)
              AND `the gathering`'s `the public in general are invited`))

GIVEN `the gathering` IS A Gathering
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `notice and a permit are required` IF
        `it is a public assembly or public procession` `the gathering`
    AND (NOT `the gathering`'s `exempted by Ministerial order`)
    AND (    (NOT `the gathering`'s `in an unrestricted area`)
         OR  `the gathering`'s `within an enhanced security special event area`)

§§ `3 -- who is an organiser`

-- s 3(1): organising means being "responsible for holding, convening, forming or collecting" the assembly or procession, and
-- includes (a) anyone who "assists or promotes" it and (b) anyone who will receive revenue from ticket sales, "but does not include a
-- person carrying on a demonstration by himself or herself or marching alone". (2): such a person is TAKING PART.
GIVEN `holds, convenes, forms or collects it` IS A BOOLEAN, `assists or promotes it` IS A BOOLEAN, `will receive ticket revenue` IS A BOOLEAN, `is demonstrating or marching alone` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an organiser` IF
        (`holds, convenes, forms or collects it` OR `assists or promotes it` OR `will receive ticket revenue`)
    AND (NOT `is demonstrating or marching alone`)

§§ `16, 17 -- organising or taking part without a permit, or off the notified date, time or route`

-- s 16(1)(a), (2)(a): each person who organises, or takes part in, a public assembly or procession "in respect of which no permit
-- has been granted ... or no such permit is in force, where a permit is required by this Act". (6): the section does not apply to an
-- exempted assembly or one in an unrestricted area outside an enhanced security special event area.
-- s 17(1): "a defence for the person charged to prove that the person did not know, and neither suspected nor had reason to
-- suspect" that no permit was in force.
GIVEN `the gathering` IS A Gathering, `a permit is in force` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no knowledge or reason to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the no-permit offence` IF
        `notice and a permit are required` `the gathering`
    AND (NOT `a permit is in force`)
    AND (NOT `proved no knowledge or reason to suspect`)

-- s 16(1)(b), (2)(b): held on a date or time, or along a route, that differs from the notice under s 6.
-- s 17(2): a defence to prove (a) no knowledge or reason to suspect the difference, or (b) the difference arose from (i)
-- circumstances beyond control, (ii) compliance with permit conditions, or (iii) "something done with the agreement of a police
-- officer not below the rank of sergeant or by the senior police officer's direction under section 8(4)".
DECLARE Rank IS ONE OF
    `no police officer`
    `constable`
    `corporal`
    `sergeant`
    `inspector or above`

GIVEN `the rank` IS A Rank
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is at least a sergeant` IF
    CONSIDER `the rank`
    WHEN `sergeant` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `inspector or above` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `did not know or suspect the difference` IS A BOOLEAN, `beyond the person's control` IS A BOOLEAN, `done to comply with a permit condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `agreed by an officer of rank` IS A Rank, `directed by the senior police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a defence to a deviation charge` IF
        `did not know or suspect the difference`
    OR  `beyond the person's control`
    OR  `done to comply with a permit condition`
    OR  `is at least a sergeant` `agreed by an officer of rank`
    OR  `directed by the senior police officer`

-- s 16(3), (5): a "repeat offender" has been convicted of a s 16(1) or (2) offence (or the pre-2009 equivalents) "on at least one
-- other occasion within the period of 5 years immediately before the date on which the person is convicted" of the current
-- offence. Measured here in years between the two conviction dates; exactly 5 years is read as within (an assumption).
GIVEN `has an earlier conviction` IS A BOOLEAN, `years from the earlier to the current conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a repeat offender` IF
        `has an earlier conviction`
    AND `years from the earlier to the current conviction` AT MOST 5

§§ `19 -- immunity for a lawful participant`

-- s 19: if the assembly or procession "(a) is the subject of a permit; (b) is peaceful; and (c) is held in accordance with the
-- conditions imposed on the permit", a participant does not, "merely because of his or her taking part, incur any civil or criminal
-- liability because of the obstruction of a public place".
GIVEN `has a permit` IS A BOOLEAN, `is peaceful` IS A BOOLEAN, `held in accordance with the permit conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `participants are immune from obstruction liability` IF
    `has a permit` AND `is peaceful` AND `held in accordance with the permit conditions`

§§ `6A -- special notice of a large event`

-- s 6A(1): "Without affecting section 6", special notice must be given by the event organiser of ANY event "(whether or not
-- comprising or involving an assembly or a procession)" if the organiser "reasonably expects more than a prescribed number of
-- individuals to participate in or to attend the event at any time". (4): different numbers for different classes of events. The
-- prescribed number is in regulations, not in the Act.
GIVEN `expected attendance at any one time` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `special notice is required` IF
    `expected attendance at any one time` GREATER THAN `the prescribed number`

§§ `7(2)(h), (4) -- the foreign-participation ground`

-- s 7(2)(h): the Commissioner may refuse a permit if there is reasonable ground for apprehending the assembly or procession may "be
-- directed towards a political end and be organised by, or involve the participation of ... (i) an entity that is not a Singapore
-- entity; (ii) an individual who is not a citizen of Singapore".
-- s 7(4): a "Singapore-controlled corporation" (a) is incorporated under written law in Singapore, (b) has a management body the
-- majority of whose members are citizens, and (c) has a majority of members (or, with share capital, of shares held by) citizens
-- or Singapore entities.
GIVEN `incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `majority of the board are citizens` IS A BOOLEAN, `majority of members or shares held by citizens or Singapore entities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Singapore-controlled corporation` IF
    `incorporated in Singapore` AND `majority of the board are citizens` AND `majority of members or shares held by citizens or Singapore entities`

GIVEN `directed towards a political end` IS A BOOLEAN, `involves an entity that is not a Singapore entity` IS A BOOLEAN, `involves an individual who is not a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreign-participation ground is open` IF
        `directed towards a political end`
    AND (`involves an entity that is not a Singapore entity` OR `involves an individual who is not a citizen`)

§§ `9, 11 -- permit duration and appeal`

-- s 9(c): a permit is valid for the particular assembly or procession, or "for the period (not exceeding one year) specified in the
-- permit".
GIVEN `months specified in the permit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the permit period is within the limit` IF
    `months specified in the permit` AT MOST 12

-- s 11(1): a person aggrieved by the Commissioner's decision "(a) to refuse to grant a permit; (b) to cancel a permit; or (c) to
-- impose any particular condition on a permit" may appeal "within 7 days after being notified of the decision (or a longer period
-- that the Minister allows in exceptional circumstances, whether before or after the end of the 7 days)". The Minister's decision
-- is final. (4): not for a cancellation under s 10(3) (a special authorisation under the Public Order and Safety (Special Powers)
-- Act 2018). A refusal to accept shorter notice (s 6(4), (5)) is not in the list; reading it as unappealable under s 11 is an
-- inference from its absence.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusal of a permit`
    `cancellation of a permit by written notice`
    `a condition imposed on a permit`
    `refusal to accept shorter notice`
    `cancellation by a special authorisation`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is appealable` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusal of a permit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cancellation of a permit by written notice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a condition imposed on a permit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `days since notified` IS A NUMBER, `the Minister allowed a longer period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal to the Minister lies` IF
        `the decision is appealable` `the decision`
    AND (`days since notified` AT MOST 7 OR `the Minister allowed a longer period`)

§§ `34 to 37 -- directions to move on`

-- s 34(1): Part 4 applies to all public places and prescribed places; (2) "This Part does not apply to any assembly or procession
-- that is not unlawful under Part 2."
-- s 35(1): the behaviour must be reasonably suspected to be interfering with trade or business, disorderly, indecent, offensive or
-- threatening, disrupting an event, or about to commit / committing an offence.
-- s 36(1): "a police officer of or above the rank of sergeant" may give a "written direction that is reasonable in the
-- circumstances". (2): not one that "interferes with a person's right of peaceful assembly unless it is reasonably necessary in the
-- interests of (a) public safety; (b) public order; or (c) the protection of the rights and freedoms of other persons". (4): to stay
-- away for "a stated reasonable time of not more than 24 hours".
-- s 37: contravening it without reasonable excuse -- $20,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE MoveOn HAS
    `rank of the officer` IS A Rank
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `behaviour of a kind in section 35 is suspected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is in an assembly or procession not unlawful under Part 2` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours the person must stay away` IS A NUMBER
    `interferes with peaceful assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reasonably necessary for public safety, public order or others' rights` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the direction` IS A MoveOn
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the move-on direction is within power` IF
        `is at least a sergeant` (`the direction`'s `rank of the officer`)
    AND `the direction`'s `in writing`
    AND `the direction`'s `behaviour of a kind in section 35 is suspected`
    AND (NOT `the direction`'s `the person is in an assembly or procession not unlawful under Part 2`)
    AND `the direction`'s `hours the person must stay away` AT MOST 24
    AND (    (NOT `the direction`'s `interferes with peaceful assembly`)
         OR  `the direction`'s `reasonably necessary for public safety, public order or others' rights`)

§§ `38 -- films of law enforcement`

-- s 38(1), (2)(a): "Any police officer of or above the rank of sergeant, or any CPIB officer, narcotics officer, intelligence officer
-- or immigration officer" who reasonably believes a film or picture "containing a record of any law enforcement activities", if
-- exhibited or communicated, "(d) prejudices the effective conduct of an ongoing law enforcement operation or investigation, or any
-- intelligence operation; or (e) endangers or will endanger the safety of any law enforcement officer" in one, may direct the
-- person to stop and to delete or surrender it. (4): failing to comply -- $20,000 or 12 months or both.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `police constable or corporal`
    `police sergeant or above`
    `CPIB officer`
    `narcotics officer`
    `intelligence officer`
    `immigration officer`
    `auxiliary police officer`

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an officer who may act under section 38` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `police constable or corporal` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `auxiliary police officer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer, `records law enforcement activities` IS A BOOLEAN, `reasonably believed to prejudice an ongoing operation or endanger an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may direct the film to be deleted or surrendered` IF
        `is an officer who may act under section 38` `the officer`
    AND `records law enforcement activities`
    AND `reasonably believed to prejudice an ongoing operation or endanger an officer`

§§ `42 -- owner or occupier of premises`

-- s 42: where the owner or occupier "is given notice by any police officer that the assembly or procession is unlawful under
-- Part 2, and such assembly or procession does take place on those premises", the owner or occupier is guilty of an offence ($5,000)
-- "unless he or she took all reasonable measures and exercised all due diligence to prevent" it.
GIVEN `given police notice that it is unlawful` IS A BOOLEAN, `it took place on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `took all reasonable measures and due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner or occupier commits an offence` IF
        `given police notice that it is unlawful`
    AND `it took place on the premises`
    AND (NOT `took all reasonable measures and due diligence`)

§§ `6A(5), 15, 16, 18, 37, 38(4), 41, 42 -- penalties and composition`

-- s 6A(5): $20,000 or 12 months or both. s 15(1) organising a prohibited assembly: $10,000 or 6 months or both; (2) taking part:
-- $5,000. s 16(1) organising without a permit etc.: $5,000; (2) taking part: $3,000; (3) repeat offender: organiser $10,000 or
-- 6 months or both, participant $5,000. s 16(4) knowingly failing to comply with a senior police officer's direction: organiser
-- $10,000, participant $5,000. s 18 disorder or obstructing an ambulance etc. at a permitted assembly: $10,000 or 6 months or
-- both. s 37 and s 38(4): $20,000 or 12 months or both. s 42: $5,000.
-- s 41(1): a prescribed offence may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of" (a) "one half of the amount of the maximum
-- fine" and (b) $5,000. Which offences are prescribed as compoundable is in regulations, not retrieved.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to give special notice of a large event`
    `organising a prohibited assembly`
    `taking part in a prohibited assembly`
    `organising without a permit`
    `taking part without a permit`
    `organising without a permit as a repeat offender`
    `taking part without a permit as a repeat offender`
    `organiser disobeying a senior police officer's direction`
    `participant disobeying a senior police officer's direction`
    `obstructing an ambulance at a permitted assembly`
    `contravening a move-on direction`
    `failing to delete or surrender a film`
    `owner or occupier allowing an unlawful assembly`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to give special notice of a large event` THEN 20000
    WHEN `organising a prohibited assembly` THEN 10000
    WHEN `taking part in a prohibited assembly` THEN 5000
    WHEN `organising without a permit` THEN 5000
    WHEN `taking part without a permit` THEN 3000
    WHEN `organising without a permit as a repeat offender` THEN 10000
    WHEN `taking part without a permit as a repeat offender` THEN 5000
    WHEN `organiser disobeying a senior police officer's direction` THEN 10000
    WHEN `participant disobeying a senior police officer's direction` THEN 5000
    WHEN `obstructing an ambulance at a permitted assembly` THEN 10000
    WHEN `contravening a move-on direction` THEN 20000
    WHEN `failing to delete or surrender a film` THEN 20000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to give special notice of a large event` THEN 12
    WHEN `organising a prohibited assembly` THEN 6
    WHEN `organising without a permit as a repeat offender` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing an ambulance at a permitted assembly` THEN 6
    WHEN `contravening a move-on direction` THEN 12
    WHEN `failing to delete or surrender a film` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
